{"title":"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An infinite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/75029a3be60a6f42198d4f3d8783722e92b20fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0, x_1, x_2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"11\" /> of real numbers is said to be <i>bounded</i> if there is a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d289ec1e0d54ba2995f2c5026cc86d50a9ff3ac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_i| \\leq  C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5cacadeebad0c1150a3d2886ab09196896f72a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Given any real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735b4fd08c7f1e4d6d79c161a483417073efb9b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, construct a bounded infinite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06eda833bf316551e618312d7e27e61cb65325a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0,x_1,x_2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"11\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c60019b7f6535233fc2dfb39cd71ea73042ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_i-x_j|\\cdot |i-j|^a\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" /> for every pair of distinct nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d9dbe8588e6243350fc642973b9365304100da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8726d98aced2f3140dd77a2d8614c2e7674700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, the series <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/064d136482774a835626f9ce6647bf8f0a6927b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty\\frac{1}{k^a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"49\" height=\"48\" /> is convergent; let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of this convergent series. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb7ae6f05388abcc2624aa206fb8d1d04ca45c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I\\subset \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> be the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d7961bb49e9a115ef7cd16c61b6d0878505adc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-L,L]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> (or any bounded subset of measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4b89ecf9b6896902dcb004ec4c6cc330c0f2fe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\geq 2L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />).\n</p><p><br />\nSuppose that we have chosen points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7ff53e4e66ae49b7c768aec10cd52d6b11a4b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"11\" /> satisfying \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3c65c8f272e28cae981865c901883961fba032e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\qquad(\\ast)\\quad |x_i-x_j|\\cdot |i-j|^a\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"242\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>for all distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356e4ac174927899efe71735b0a268831e69e5e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j&lt;m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />. We show that we can choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b729c3085357c3ee742e5e61379892589d8c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_m\\in I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/3/4c303797eb8aa7fc29549dc0bcbf10dc797c0d4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\ast)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> holds for all distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/6442302096d87c3405bedbc44ca50a9ed3c7e079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j\\leq m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />. The only new cases are when one number (WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />) is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, so we must guarantee that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/1064e65bf18c34f8d3c8a4bdd0a7244b0ce0c52d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_m-x_j|\\cdot |m-j|^a\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd0210dd19b146a23e1e4ca300f8461c1369ef1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq j&lt;m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a0b1af5ad95dbbf12009ff64c0f24f727682e4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> be the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b8bfc9781773611f5b0696e6e00aa7aa3c5cdf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_j-\\frac{1}{|m-j|^a},x_j+\\frac{1}{|m-j|^a})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"237\" height=\"41\" />, of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/4989a19f4adeb7b88716b0be54758346797f450b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{|m-j|^a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"67\" height=\"41\" />. The points that are valid choices for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fcaeea91c5bea53f0f7fb9dc6300816e6320b58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" /> are precisely the points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61f33afa855388c55e5e715f7768ba22fde87011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I\\setminus(U_0\\cup \\cdots \\cup U_{m-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />, so we must show that this set is nonempty. The total length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3eacd6e309c23809ee0e59dcbe84d5871c13156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu(U_0\\cup \\cdot\\cup U_{m-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" /> is at most the sum of the lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c0088effe0b5ee63c3d95472f9329fc3fe1cff05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu(U_0)+\\cdots+\\mu(U_{m-1})=\\frac{2}{m^a}+\\frac{2}{(m-1)^a}+\\cdots+\\frac{2}{2^a}+\\frac{2}{1^a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"454\" height=\"41\" />. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de4e53994815c34597e45bf734fe21d42d8d43e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sum_{k=1}^m\\frac{1}{k^a}&lt;2\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\frac{1}{k^a}=2L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"195\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore the total measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15fa5e51e89e3214c696b89257350144829da004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U_0\\cup \\cdots \\cup U_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/5/4b5e0fce7dc756875f54ece303513c45f4ba1708.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;2L=\\mu(I)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61f33afa855388c55e5e715f7768ba22fde87011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I\\setminus(U_0\\cup \\cdots \\cup U_{m-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" /> has positive measure and thus is nonempty. Choosing any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea8027643c98cd4f8b60d74211a290dba291f04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_m\\in I\\setminus(U_0\\cup \\cdots \\cup U_{m-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" /> and continuing by induction constructs the desired sequence.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The argument above would not work for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/edd9561dbb89971d62a511f52bd213941441ef53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\textstyle\\sum \\frac{1}{k^a}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"39\" height=\"21\" /> only converges for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8726d98aced2f3140dd77a2d8614c2e7674700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. But Osmun Nal argues <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3v3CMQS_5Cc\">in this video</a> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e6ed04c622004086ecf7a381b8d12db294f1c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k=C\\cdot\\left(k\\sqrt{2}-\\lfloor k\\sqrt{2}\\rfloor\\right), C=2\\sqrt2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"315\" height=\"34\" /> satisfies the stronger inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/612181a5961d7dd0298394c58014e54ddf22a280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_i-x_j|\\cdot |i-j|\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" /> for all distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d9dbe8588e6243350fc642973b9365304100da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" />; in other words, this sequence simultaneously solves the problem for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/261483393788c1276a45334b5f5a196dae556b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> simultaneously.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a5360887e67ba189cc63594faf999abfa355933.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\max \\left( \\left\\lceil \\dfrac{1}{a - 1} \\right\\rceil, 3 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"186\" height=\"45\" />, then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aa2782a45c31eecc05ebe961026c93b3b7bcdd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\ln \\left( n + 1 \\right)}{\\ln n} = \\dfrac{\\ln n + \\ln \\left( 1 + 1/n \\right)}{\\ln n} &lt; \\dfrac{\\ln n + 1/n}{\\ln n} = 1 + \\dfrac{1}{n \\ln n} &lt; 1 + \\dfrac{1}{n} \\le a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"568\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4e083a77d4a4de2c785ba7c6cc2c5efe4d90b72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^a &gt; n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>For any non-negative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, represent it as base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positional notation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/817ac542d12569d0432f5fc6eadfb923142bb676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = i_m n^m + i_{m-1} n^{m-1} + \\cdots + i_2 n^2 + i_1 n + i_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"354\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2ac561b22aa533a9bc5684c6baa900334643320d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_m, i_{m-1}, \\cdots, i_2, i_1, i_0 \\in \\left\\{ 0, 1, 2, \\cdots, n - 1 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"335\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We directly construct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4a05aacaed0cfbd3ff9f0b399086cba5993c37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = n \\left( i_0 + i_1 \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-1} + i_2 \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-2} + \\cdots + i_m \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-m} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"484\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p>We allow leading zeros for representing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> due to the leading zeros do not effect the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f054470668af3059fa503b1f67547da1f3e8311f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le x_i \\le n \\left( \\left( n - 1 \\right) + \\left( n - 1 \\right) \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-1} + \\cdots + \\left( n - 1 \\right) \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-m} \\right) &lt; n \\left( n - 1 \\right) \\dfrac{1}{1 - \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-1}} = n^2 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"808\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d6511b55b27d5ca7a44eecbe3b4810dcb1384d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| x_i \\right| &lt; n^2 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" />, which is bounded\n</p><p>For any two distinct non-negative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/743293b410b7d3bdf6a048265134ab7aa60b38b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\neq j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />, represent them as base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positional notation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/817ac542d12569d0432f5fc6eadfb923142bb676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = i_m n^m + i_{m-1} n^{m-1} + \\cdots + i_2 n^2 + i_1 n + i_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"354\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4f3f850ed88fbd025a721bc1dfe59e75617fd52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j = j_m n^m + j_{m-1} n^{m-1} + \\cdots + j_2 n^2 + j_1 n + j_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"362\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496806fe42452d72e039b446f4c3c59fb801cbf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_m, i_{m-1}, \\cdots, i_2, i_1, i_0, j_m, j_{m-1}, \\cdots, j_2, j_1, j_0 \\in \\left\\{ 0, 1, 2, \\cdots, n - 1 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"513\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> be the minimum number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060af3a0563b30225bb05c591b34a86bd5ec851b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_\\ell \\neq j_\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d11ee8a50ac357e1157d2dc0886d105e49e34d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_0 = j_0, i_1 = j_1, \\cdots, i_{\\ell - 1} = j_{\\ell - 1}, i_\\ell \\neq j_\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"303\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79d45af2c545b0ac1499bc3f9a5895b1c42bbbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| i - j \\right| \\ge n^\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>Without loss of generality, assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df261cdf3433ed22f4e438800f94d92b31241cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_\\ell &gt; j_\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06a92e69103f31bfb4506e6292314f1b70677b07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_\\ell - j_\\ell \\ge 1, j_{\\ell + 1} - i_{\\ell + 1}, j_{\\ell + 2} - i_{\\ell + 2}, \\cdots, j_m - i_m \\le n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"436\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba57f1d27e7320fbfcce5497a72263ce56a0c334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| x_i - x_j \\right| = n \\left( \\left( i_\\ell - j_\\ell \\right) \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell} - \\left( j_{\\ell+1} - i_{\\ell+1} \\right) \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell-1} - \\left( j_{\\ell+2} - i_{\\ell+2} \\right) \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell-2} - \\cdots - \\left( j_m - i_m \\right) \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-m} \\right) \\\\~\\\\ \\ge n \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell} - n \\left( n - 1 \\right) \\left( \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell-1} + \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell-2} + \\cdots + \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-m} \\right) \\\\~\\\\ &gt; n \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell} - n \\left( n - 1 \\right) \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell-1} \\dfrac{1}{1 - \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-1}} = \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"130\" />\n</p><p>Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/9292c4363a5f4dac81a41676a4280966597fe8a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| x_i - x_j \\right| \\left| i - j \\right|^a &gt; \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell} n^{a \\ell} &gt; \\left( n + 1 \\right)^{-\\ell} \\left( n + 1 \\right)^\\ell = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"447\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~Joseph Tsai, mgtsai@gmail.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO\" title=\"1991 IMO\">1991 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1991 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017182844\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 378/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 866/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14596/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.042      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    8.042      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16905:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017182844 and revision id 212524. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}